		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Je ne pense vraiment pas que ce soit un problème d&#039;écriture du mot de passe: j&#039;utilise les caractères comme &quot;6Me:=&quot;, ce qui est standard.</p><p>Comment puis-je savoir les instances démarrées ?<br />Dans &quot;ps -aux&quot; j&#039;ai les lignes :<br />root&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 11009&#160; 0.0&#160; 0.3&#160; &#160;9996&#160; 3428 ?&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; Ss&#160; &#160;16:16&#160; &#160;0:00 sshd: postgres [priv]<br />postgres 11100&#160; 0.0&#160; 0.1&#160; &#160;9996&#160; 1572 ?&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; S&#160; &#160; 16:17&#160; &#160;0:00 sshd: postgres@pts/1<br />...<br />postgres 18259&#160; 0.0&#160; 0.7&#160; 49756&#160; 7844 ?&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; S&#160; &#160; Sep14&#160; &#160;0:13 /usr/lib/postgresql/9.1/bin/postgres -D /var/lib/postgresql/9.1<br />postgres 18261&#160; 0.0&#160; 0.1&#160; 49756&#160; 2040 ?&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; Ss&#160; &#160;Sep14&#160; &#160;0:15 postgres: writer process&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; <br />postgres 18262&#160; 0.0&#160; 0.1&#160; 49756&#160; 1432 ?&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; Ss&#160; &#160;Sep14&#160; &#160;0:15 postgres: wal writer process&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; <br />postgres 18263&#160; 0.0&#160; 0.2&#160; 50468&#160; 2696 ?&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; Ss&#160; &#160;Sep14&#160; &#160;0:12 postgres: autovacuum launcher process&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;<br />postgres 18264&#160; 0.0&#160; 0.1&#160; 20260&#160; 1560 ?&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; Ss&#160; &#160;Sep14&#160; &#160;0:16 postgres: stats collector process</p>]]></content>
